478 0 obj
<</Title(Round-robin \(repair option 1\): task i is assigned to worker \(i mod worker_count\). The expensive early tasks are spread across workers while retaining static assignment and low coordination overhead.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 431 0 R/Prev 494 0 R/Next 461 0 R>>
endobj

479 0 obj
<</Title(Immediate cause: equal numbers of tasks were assigned without considering their unequal computational costs.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 446 0 R/Prev 462 0 R/Next 480 0 R>>
endobj

480 0 obj
<</Title(Root cause: the scheduling policy assumes task-count equality is a valid proxy for work equality. That assumption is false for a cost-skewed task list. The distributor creates a long tail of unfinished work on one worker, reducing effective parallelism.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 446 0 R/Prev 479 0 R/Next 463 0 R>>
endobj

481 0 obj
<</Title(Option A \204 Round-robin static assignment. Advantages: deterministic, low coordination overhead, simple to reproduce, and spreads the front-loaded expensive tasks in this workload. Limitations: it may be less effective if task costs have a periodic pattern or are not known in advance.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 464 0 R/Next 495 0 R>>
endobj

482 0 obj
<</Title(Selected design: keep block as the deliberately failing baseline; compare round-robin and dynamic as repaired alternatives. Round-robin is the simple primary repair for the ordered workload. Dynamic is retained to test whether runtime balancing is worth its queue overhead.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 464 0 R/Prev 496 0 R>>
endobj

483 0 obj
<</Title(7. Selected Design and Invariants)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 464 0 R/First 497 0 R/Last 498 0 R/Count -5/Next 465 0 R>>
endobj

484 0 obj
<</Title(The supplied ca3_multicore_scheduler_debug.py implements the defective block baseline and the two alternatives. It supports affinity modes none, spread and single, and distributions block, rr and dynamic.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 465 0 R/First 499 0 R/Last 499 0 R/Count -1/Next 500 0 R>>
endobj

485 0 obj
<</Title(The code uses multiprocessing so CPU-bound work can execute in separate processes rather than being serialized by the standard CPython Global Interpreter Lock. It uses Linux os.sched_getaffinity and os.sched_setaffinity for CPU placement.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 465 0 R/Prev 500 0 R>>
endobj

