endobj

495 0 obj
<</Title(Option B \204 Dynamic chunk queue. Advantages: workers that finish early can obtain more work; it adapts to variable task costs. Limitations: queue synchronization, inter-process communication and chunk-size choices add overhead. Very small chunks can cause excessive coordination.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 464 0 R/Prev 481 0 R/Next 496 0 R>>
endobj

496 0 obj
<</Title(Option C \204 Cost-aware static partitioning. Estimate or know task costs, then distribute tasks so each worker receives a similar total estimated cost. Advantages: can balance predictable workloads with little runtime coordination. Limitations: requires cost estimates and may be inaccurate when task durations vary at runtime.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 464 0 R/Prev 495 0 R/Next 482 0 R>>
endobj

497 0 obj
<</Title(Correctness invariant 1 \204 Task conservation: every task ID from 0 to N\2121 must be completed exactly once.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 483 0 R/Next 505 0 R>>
endobj

498 0 obj
<</Title(Performance metrics: wall-clock completion time; throughput \(completed tasks / wall seconds\); worker CPU-time imbalance \(maximum worker CPU time / mean worker CPU time\); and, optionally, Linux context switches and CPU migrations from perf.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 483 0 R/Prev 506 0 R>>
endobj

499 0 obj
<</Title(25PCCS201 | TADIGOTLA VASANTH DIWAKAR)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 484 0 R>>
endobj

